Title: How to create single request object from multiple queries input arguments?
Description: I am working on migrating legacy use cases to our new `GraphQL` service. 

- Internally all our requests gets mapped to single `ProcessRequest` object which holds all input arguments being passed from Schema. 
- Then we pass this `ProcessRequest` object to underlying methods which in turn returns back `ProcessResponse` object which has response for that request.

Below is `ProcessRequest` class:

    public interface IProcess
    {
        int ClientId { get; set; }
        int LanguageId { get; set; }
        int CustomerId { get; set; }
    }

    public interface IData
    {
        IList<Filter> Filters { get; set; }
        KeywordsTemplate KeywordsTemplate { get; set; }
    }

    public class Filter
    {
        public string Key { get; set; }
        public int Value { get; set; }
    }

    public class KeywordsTemplate
    {
        public string Query { get; set; }
        public string UserQuery { get; set; }
    }

    public class ClientType
    {
        public string ClientKey { get; set; }
    }

    public class Shop
    {
        public double CartAmount { get; set; }
        public double PromoAmount { get; set; }
        public IList<int> ClientIds { get; set; }
    }

    public class ListingRequest
    {
        public IList<Filter> Filters { get; set; }
        public int ClientNumber { get; set; }
        public string PotType { get; set; }
        public IList<int> ClientIds { get; set; }
    }

    public class ListingsRequest
    {
        public IList<ListingRequest> Listings { get; set; }
    }

    public class ProcessRequest : IData, IProcess
    {
        public DetailsRequest DetailsRequest { get; set; }
        public ClientType ClientType { get; set; }
        public ListingsRequest ListingsRequest { get; set; }
        public ProtoRequest ProtoRequest { get; set; }

        public IList<Filter> Filters { get; set; }
        public KeywordsTemplate KeywordsTemplate { get; set; }
        public int ClientId { get; set; }
    }

For my below `GraphQL` query - I map input arguments to my `ProcessRequest` class and then call corresponding methods to get `ProcessResponse` object. Then I created a corresponding model `LandingGroup` from `ProcessResponse` class which exactly matches with what I need in `GraphQL` response for my below `contentRequest` query and then I use that in my `ContentResponseType` class to get what I need.

    {
      contentRequest(clientId: 123, filters: [{key: "abc", value: "98"}], clientKey: "process") {
        title
        id
        name
      }
    }

Below is how I am using my Query -

    public class TitanQuery : ObjectGraphType<object>
    {
        public TitanQuery(....)
        {
            Name = "Query";

            FieldAsync<ListGraphType<ContentResponseType>>(
                "contentRequest",
                arguments: new QueryArguments(
                        new QueryArgument<NonNullGraphType<IntGraphType>>
                        {
                            Name = "clientId",
                            Description = "Client Id of the request"

                        },
                        new QueryArgument<ListGraphType<FilterType>>
                        {
                            Name = "filters",
                            Description = "Filters"
                        },
                        new QueryArgument<StringGraphType>
                        {
                            Name = "clientKey",
                            DefaultValue = "abc",
                            Description = "some stuff"
                        }
                    ),

                resolve: async context =>
                {
                    var clientId = context.GetArgument<int>("clientId");
                    var filters = context.GetArgument<List<Filter>>("filters");
                    var clientKey = context.GetArgument<string>("clientKey");

                    // mapping all the arguments to ProcessRequest class
                    ProcessRequest processRequest = new ProcessRequest()
                    {
                        ClientId = clientId,
                        Filters = filters,
                        ClientType = new ClientType()
                        {
                            ClientKey = clientKey
                        },
                        ProtoRequest = new ProtoRequest()
                    };

                    // below line returns 'ProcessResponse' object by using 'processRequest' object
                    var processResponse = await metadataService.ProcessData(processRequest);

                    var dataGroups = processResponse.LandingResponse.DataGroups.Select(dataGroup => new LandingGroup
                    {
                        DataGroup = dataGroup,
                        TileContext = processResponse.TileContext
                    });

                    return dataGroups;
                }
            );
        }
    }

**Problem Statement**

Everything works fine for my above single schema use case. Now I have a very different use case with multiple schemas as shown below. I am not able to figure out on how to do it or whether it is even possible to do it? As you can see below I have three different schemas. 

- All the input arguments from below queries maps to single `ProcessRequest` object. 
- And then I get single `ProcessResponse` object back from `ProcessRequest` object like the same old way as shown above in the `TitanQuery` class.
- All the GraphQL response fields for each schema is already there in `ProcessResponse` object so I need to find a way to return all those fields back to `GraphQL` response for each query.
- `clientId`, `filters` will be there in all the schemas with same values. They will map to corresponding field in `ProcessRequest` class.

Below is my query with multiple schemas:

    {
      contentRequest(clientId: 123, filters: [{key: "hello", value: "98"}], clientKey: "process") {
        title
        id
        name
      }
      find(queryString: "", filters: [{key: "hello", value: "98"}], clientId: 1234) {
        metricx {
          name
          key
        }
        prodCount
      }
      itemListings(pots: [{potType: "KITE_1", filters: [{key: "c", value: "1341"}]}, {potType: "KITE_2", filters: [{key: "c", value: "9812"}]}], filters: [{key: "hello", value: "98"}], clientId: 1234, clientKey: "process") {
        potType
        productAlgo
        count
        listingEndpoint
      }
    }

Now my question is how can I make single `ProcessRequest` object by extracting input arguments from all my above queries? And then from single `ProcessResponse` object I need to extract all those fields which each of my query needs in `GraphQL` response. Also I am not sure if we can have different models from `ProcessResponse` object for different combinations of schemas and use them?

**Note:**

- I have simplified my response fields for each query to make it easier for understanding but in general they are complicated with lot of fields but all of those fields for each query are part of `ProcessResponse` object only.
- Also this is our legacy use case which we are migrating to our new `GraphQL` service and that legacy service passes queries in that format as of now so we are trying to follow the same format if we can.


